<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109479" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόφᾰσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a being half seen,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τῶν ὀφθαλμῶν,</span> of the eyes,
			when in sleep they show through the half-opened eyelids, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prog.</u>
				2
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποφαύσιας</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aph.</u>
				6.52
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SA</u>
				1.5
			</span></i>; <i>trace, slight indication,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱδρῶτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					10.541
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>symptom, sign,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρησταὶ ὑποφάσιες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>CA</u>
					1.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>appearance,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σολοικισμοῦ ὑπόφασιν ποιεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Pron.</u>
					22.22
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲ ὑ.</span> not a <i>trace,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				84
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ὑ. τῶν μερῶν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				157
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
